preConditionHook:
// THE HEADLINE BROOKS TRAIL. While long, the protective stop sits just below the
// most recent CONFIRMED swing low and moves with each new pivot; mirrored above
// the most recent swing high while short. Nine mined candidates from all three
// volumes collapse into this one rule.
//
// Not TrailingStop / AtrTrailingStop, which trail a dollar or ATR distance below
// the position's PEAK PROFIT: on a trend that pauses the dollar trail tightens
// with every new high while this one does not move until a new pivot confirms.
// Not StopBeyondRecentRangeExtreme, whose level is an N-bar lowest low
// taken through the previous bar -- a Donchian floor that moves every bar the
// window rolls, where a pivot is a chart
// structure that only changes when one forms. Not SwingPivotTarget, which is a
// profit target at the OPPOSING pivot (a long exits at the swing high); this is a
// stop at the SAME-side pivot. Not InitialStopBeyondSwingAtEntry, which freezes
// the pivot that existed at entry.
//
// FOUR SOURCES ADD "only after the market makes a new high", which is dropped as
// redundant: a fresh swing low only becomes the most recent one after a rally, so
// the trigger adds no bars and would cost a Highest() call site.
//
// THE LEVEL IS READ FRESH EVERY BAR AND IS NOT RATCHETED. Brooks phrases it as
// "raise the stop", but the merged pseudocode is the plain read, and a per
// position monotone ratchet is exactly the machinery TrailStopBehindStrongBar and
// StopBeyondExtremeSinceEntry already carry -- adding it here would make this the
// same machine at a different reference and would need an at-entry seed the
// sources do not give. A deeper pullback that prints a LOWER swing low therefore
// widens the stop.
//
// THE PIVOT SCAN IS INLINED from SwingHigh per the B-list decision, at
// Occurrence 1. MEASURED (EL_Swing_Probe.txt / el_swing_output1.txt, @ES 60 min):
// the pivot test is MIXED -- at-or-beyond the pivotStrength OLDER bars, STRICTLY
// beyond the pivotStrength NEWER bars, and bars-ago indexing makes the SMALLER
// index the NEWER bar, so the strict half is the pk < pj loop; the confirmation
// lag is exactly pivotStrength bars, never 0 or 1, so the level is knowable
// without lookahead and during the lag the PREVIOUS pivot is reported;
// lookbackBars is EL's Length, offsets 0..lookbackBars-1 inclusive, and the
// neighbourhood test reaches pivotStrength bars PAST the window, so the deepest
// bar touched is lookbackBars - 1 + pivotStrength; an empty window returns the -1
// SENTINEL, guarded because -1 as a PRICE sits under every real price and would
// take every long off; the comparisons carry the 2.22e-12 relational tolerance,
// hence el_lt / el_le / el_gt / el_ge. The low side's tie sense is the mirror of
// the measured high-side rule. No WFSafe_SwingLow exists, so plain EL governs.
// Both scans run unconditionally every bar, so Max Bars Back covers them and the
// EasyLanguage call sites advance on the same bars.
//
// lookbackBars is not in the merged parameter list and is what makes the pivot
// window addressable; 40 is the corpus default (SwingPivotTarget,
// ShrinkingSwingIncrementsExit). Offsets are one tick everywhere in the sources,
// and the tick is written division-first, trailOffsetTicks * (ctx.MinMove() /
// ctx.PriceScale()), read once per bar into a local since MinMove and PriceScale
// are per-symbol constants for the whole run.
//
// Every scratch value is a localVariables entry, never a hook-scope declaration,
// so the hooks survive a double placement.
tickSize = ctx.MinMove() / ctx.PriceScale();
lo1 = -1.0;
for (pj = (int)pivotStrength; pj <= (int)lookbackBars - 1; ++pj) {
    pok = true;
    for (pk = pj - (int)pivotStrength; pk < pj; ++pk) {
        if (!el_lt(low[pj], low[pk])) { pok = false; break; }
    }
    if (pok) {
        for (pk = pj + 1; pk <= pj + (int)pivotStrength; ++pk) {
            if (!el_le(low[pj], low[pk])) { pok = false; break; }
        }
    }
    if (pok) { lo1 = low[pj]; break; }
}
hi1 = -1.0;
for (pj = (int)pivotStrength; pj <= (int)lookbackBars - 1; ++pj) {
    pok = true;
    for (pk = pj - (int)pivotStrength; pk < pj; ++pk) {
        if (!el_gt(high[pj], high[pk])) { pok = false; break; }
    }
    if (pok) {
        for (pk = pj + 1; pk <= pj + (int)pivotStrength; ++pk) {
            if (!el_ge(high[pj], high[pk])) { pok = false; break; }
        }
    }
    if (pok) { hi1 = high[pj]; break; }
}
